WORK TASK — Restore Mission Control Browser Task Launch as Trusted Work Creator

Objective

Repair the regression introduced by the trusted-setter contract by reconnecting the existing Mission Control-controlled browser launcher to the merged Work model-routing contract.

Do not invent a new task launcher if an existing managed ChatGPT/Work browser relay already creates new chats / Work threads.

Preserve the good merged contract:

Chat-owned routing decision;

source-bound workExecutionProfile;

separate Chat-message and directive-artifact provenance;

no Work self-attestation;

no Work self-escalation;

trusted setter evidence;

receipt/finalization/telemetry binding.

The mistake was treating “no native callable task-creation API” as equivalent to “no trusted task-creation boundary.” A Mission Control-owned browser relay can itself be that trusted boundary.

Reasoning tier

This is browser/GUI execution with multi-app state, so use GPT-6 Astra Low under the current routing policy unless unavailable. Do not raise effort without a concrete execution-reasoning trigger.

Intended flow

Chat selects the exact Work profile.

Mission Control authorizes the exact source-bound directive/profile.

The existing MC-owned browser relay reuses the managed ChatGPT tab/session.

It opens New chat / the required new Work task/thread using the existing controlled flow.

It selects the source-authorized model and reasoning effort in the UI.

It reads back the visible selected model and effort from DOM/accessibility state when available.

It may capture a screenshot as calibration/audit evidence.

It submits the exact bounded Work directive.

It records the created chat/thread/task locator.

The relay, as an authenticated trusted SYSTEM boundary, emits work_task_creation_selection_applied.

Existing preflight/finalization/telemetry consume that trusted record.

A future native OpenAI task-creation API is preferable but is not a prerequisite for Mission Control task creation.

1. Find and reuse the existing browser launcher

Inspect current canonical Mission Control state and locate the component that already:

controls the authenticated ChatGPT browser;

creates new chats / Work threads;

selects model/thinking controls;

respects managed-tab reuse rules.

Do not replace it with a parallel launcher unless the old path is genuinely gone.

Relevant Universal invariant:

fresh conversation = New chat in the current verified reusable ChatGPT tab, not a new browser tab;

one managed ChatGPT tab in steady state;

private MC-owned chats only;

existing tab-count and doctor/status rules remain authoritative.

Record the exact existing implementation path before editing.

2. Trust controller provenance, not transport type

Extend/adapt work_task_creation_selection_applied so a Mission Control-owned browser relay is a valid trusted source when:

producer is authenticated SYSTEM / MC-owned relay identity;

relay controls the verified managed ChatGPT/Work session;

evidence binds the exact profile authorization + directive + task;

model/effort selection evidence comes from the relay's own UI action/readback, not Work's later claim;

created task/chat/thread locator is recorded.

Add a source such as:
TRUSTED_MANAGED_BROWSER_TASK_CREATION_BOUNDARY

Retain the structured/native source for a future API bridge.

Browser evidence should contain only bounded non-sensitive facts: IDs, exact selected model/effort, Fast request/control if exposed, producer ID, source kind, created task/thread locator, UI-readback status, optional screenshot evidence reference, timestamp.

Never store prompt bodies, cookies, credentials, session values, unrelated page text, or private screenshots in telemetry.

3. Routine proof standard

For routine SET_REQUEST_SUFFICIENT, do not require backend provider attestation.

Sufficient routine evidence:

trusted MC-owned relay performed the selection;

relay read visible selected model and effort from UI DOM/accessibility state where possible;

readback equals the authorized profile;

relay created the new task/chat/thread and recorded its locator.

Provider observedProfile may remain null.

If UI readback disagrees:

retry selection once if clearly mechanical;

read back again;

if still mismatched/ambiguous, fail closed before task submission.

No model or effort self-escalation.

4. Screenshot calibration

The owner explicitly accepts screenshot evidence as practical calibration and does not require screenshots on every routine run once the mechanism is proven.

Run 2–3 harmless bounded calibration launches, enough to cover both model families and effort switching:

Sol Medium;

Astra Low;

optionally Sol Low if needed.

For each:

reuse the canonical managed browser session/tab;

New chat / new task through the existing flow;

select exact model and effort;

capture DOM/accessibility readback;

capture a screenshot showing selection, provided it can be kept free of unrelated sensitive content;

submit a trivial harmless task sufficient to prove task creation;

record resulting task/chat/thread locator;

verify it corresponds to the intended launch.

This is not a model-quality benchmark.

After calibration passes, routine runs need only trusted relay action + UI readback + created-task locator. Screenshot again when UI/selectors materially change, readback is ambiguous, a mismatch occurs, or a formal Sol-vs-Astra comparison needs stronger provenance.

If DOM readback is unavailable but a screenshot unambiguously exposes the selected state, treat screenshot as a bounded fallback only if it can be evaluated reliably; ambiguity must fail closed.

5. Fast mode

Fast remains DO_NOT_ENABLE_FAST by default.

If current UI offers no reliable Fast setter/readback:

do not enable it;

record observed Fast as null;

do not claim it was verified off;

do not block routine execution merely because it was unobservable.

6. Restore runtime operation

Current runtime returns WORK_TASK_CREATION_BRIDGE_UNAVAILABLE because only a hypothetical native bridge was considered trusted.

Once browser relay evidence is wired in:

routine browser-created Work tasks should no longer hit that blocker;

SET_REQUEST_SUFFICIENT passes when trusted UI selection/readback evidence matches;

INDEPENDENT_READBACK_REQUIRED remains stronger and may still fail if actual provider identity cannot be independently verified.

Use an explicit runtime status such as:
BROWSER_TASK_CREATION_TRUSTED_SETTER_ACTIVE

Do not claim native API task creation exists.

7. Browser/session efficiency

Preserve:

headless by default unless visible interaction is genuinely required;

reuse browser process/context/session;

reuse current verified ChatGPT tab;

New chat means New chat in that tab;

no duplicate-tab fanout;

existing tab-count caps and doctor telemetry;

never repurpose personal/external chats.

8. Tests

Add/adjust focused regressions proving:

MC-owned browser relay SYSTEM evidence can satisfy trusted setter evidence.

WORKER cannot forge it.

Sol Medium UI action + exact UI readback passes routine preflight.

Astra Low UI action + exact UI readback passes routine preflight.

UI mismatch fails before task submission.

Wrong authorization/directive/task binding fails.

Created task/thread locator is required for browser-source evidence.

Provider observed profile may remain null.

INDEPENDENT_READBACK_REQUIRED is not weakened by browser proof.

Fast unobservability is not reported as verified off.

No self-escalation.

Source-message vs directive-artifact provenance stays intact.

New-chat flow reuses the managed tab and respects tab limits.

Browser evidence cannot leak prompt/session/credential data into telemetry.

Screenshot calibration is audit evidence, not backend provider attestation.

Existing native/structured trusted setter source remains supported.

Consumer seam:

A source-authorized model/effort profile must be selected by the Mission Control-owned browser task creator, visibly read back as the same selection, and associated with the newly created Work/chat/thread locator before task admission. Work's later claim is never evidence.

9. PR / deployment boundary

Implement on a task branch and open a PR.

Run focused/affected tests, Mission Control tests, browser-relay tests, typecheck/build, repository-required full suite, deterministic audit, archive reconstruction if affected, and hosted checks.

Do not merge before Chat reviews the live diff.
Do not deploy before Chat reviews calibration evidence.

No subscription/account changes.
No purchased credits/API spend.
No Antigravity/Jules involvement.

Final receipt

Return:

MISSION CONTROL BROWSER TASK CREATION RESTORED

with:

existing browser launcher identified;

files changed;

trusted browser evidence path;

Sol Medium calibration;

Astra Low calibration;

screenshot/evidence references;

DOM/accessibility readback used;

created task/thread locator evidence;

negative mismatch-control result;

tests/checks;

PR and head SHA;

runtime classification;

remaining limitation;

direct artifact bundle link/attachment.

Do not merge or deploy.
